    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c8cce461",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "dishwasher_birth_concept",
      "label": "dishwasher at birth",
      "description": "The phrase 'dishwasher at birth' is a pun that plays on the human concept of birth — the moment of coming into existence — and applies it to an appliance. This requires understanding that 'birth' is a biological and cultural concept reserved for living beings, and that applying it to inanimate objects is absurd and humorous. The meme relies on this conceptual incongruity for its effect.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d0991925"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5bdaab09",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "infantilization_appliance",
      "label": "infantilizing appliances",
      "description": "The meme subtly infantilizes the dishwasher by calling it 'at birth,' which is a form of anthropomorphism. This requires background knowledge about how people sometimes anthropomorphize objects (e.g., calling a car 'my baby' or a pet 'my child') and how such language can be used humorously or mockingly. The humor derives from the absurdity of treating an appliance as if it were a newborn human.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d0991925"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_afc7b7be",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "pun_based_humor",
      "label": "pun-based humor",
      "description": "The meme relies on wordplay — specifically, a pun — to create humor. The phrase 'rare picture of a dishwasher at birth' is a play on the phrase 'rare picture of a baby at birth,' which is a common trope in photography. Understanding this type of humor requires knowledge of linguistic puns and how they are used in comedy.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d0991925"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2e6ba0cb",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "absurdity_comedy",
      "label": "absurdity as comedic device",
      "description": "The humor in the meme stems from the absurdity of the situation — a dishwasher being 'born' — which is inherently illogical. This requires background knowledge about comedy techniques, particularly the use of absurdity to generate laughter. The juxtaposition of a mundane kitchen appliance with a biological concept (birth) creates the comedic effect.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d0991925"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4b880471",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "appliance_personification",
      "label": "personification of appliances",
      "description": "The meme involves personifying the dishwasher, attributing human characteristics (like being 'born') to it. This requires understanding that personification is a common rhetorical and comedic device, often used to make inanimate objects seem more relatable or to create humor through contrast with their actual nature.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d0991925"
